<title>BRAZIL: Copel 1996 net higher.</title>
<headline>Copel 1996 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Parana state power utility Copel, formally known as Companhia Paranaense de Energia, published the following statement on its 1996 results.</p>
<p>			    1996		    1995</p>
<p>    net profit	193.948 million	 97.293 million</p>
<p>    net shr	   0.8024 reais	0.4025 reais</p>
<p>    net oper revs   1.074 bln	   809.431 million</p>
<p>NOTE: All data in Brazilian reais.</p>
<p>Figures calculated under Brazilian corporate law accounting method.</p>
<p>Under the inflation-adjusted accounting method, the company said it posted a net profit of 225.2 million reais in 1996, up from 110.8 million in 1995.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 5511 2485412))</p>
